  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1026 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nNot much is different in the long term forecast. Forecast surface\nanalyses don't have anything on the horizon that could be\nqualified as a bonafide cold front in Middle TN until well beyond\nthe forecast period. PoPs are in the 40-50% range pretty much \nevery day with hot and humid afternoons. Moving into next week, \nthe airmass becomes a little more soggy and thus increases heat \nindices back into the triple digits through at least Thursday. It\nlooks pretty borderline with Heat Advisory criteria right now, so\nthis will be something to monitor on a day-to-day basis next week\nfor heat headlines. The upper level flow looks pretty much zonal \neach day, leading to a persistence forecast of afternoon showers \nand thunderstorms with hot and humid conditions through next week.",
